From: OpenWrt R18 port
Subject: MIPS: kexec: don't trip hardened usercopy on kexec_argv_buf

kexec_argv_buf lives in .text (relocate_kernel.S) so it can be copied
together with the relocation code. copy_from_user() into it is rejected
by CONFIG_HARDENED_USERCOPY ("Kernel memory overwrite attempt detected
to kernel text") and BUG()s on every `kexec -l`. The destination is a
fixed, correctly sized buffer and size is bounded above, so use
raw_copy_from_user() which skips the object check.

--- a/arch/mips/kernel/machine_kexec.c
+++ b/arch/mips/kernel/machine_kexec.c
@@ -75,7 +75,7 @@ static void machine_kexec_init_argv(struct kimage *image)
 		pr_warn("kexec command line truncated to %zd bytes\n", size);
 
 	/* Copy to kernel space */
-	if (copy_from_user(kexec_argv_buf, buf, size))
+	if (raw_copy_from_user(kexec_argv_buf, buf, size))
 		pr_warn("kexec command line copy to kernel space failed\n");
 
 	kexec_argv_buf[size - 1] = 0;
